><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250701084826+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250701084827+10'00'" name="c5dbdb36-e5db-42a5-a2bc-71c708fa3fa1" page="12" coords="271.979000,603.132000,288.419000,603.132000,271.979000,588.932000,288.419000,588.932000,45.637800,590.132000,288.429000,590.132000,45.637800,575.932000,288.429000,575.932000,45.637800,577.132000,288.439000,577.132000,45.637800,562.932000,288.439000,562.932000,45.637800,564.132000,288.428000,564.132000,45.637800,549.932000,288.428000,549.932000,45.637800,551.132000,288.439000,551.132000,45.637800,536.932000,288.439000,536.932000,45.637800,538.132000,288.428000,538.132000,45.637800,523.932000,288.428000,523.932000,45.637800,525.132000,288.423000,525.132000,45.637800,510.932000,288.423000,510.932000,45.637800,512.132000,288.449000,512.132000,45.637800,497.932000,288.449000,497.932000,45.637800,499.132000,288.429000,499.132000,45.637800,484.932000,288.429000,484.932000,45.637800,486.132000,288.428000,486.132000,45.637800,471.932000,288.428000,471.932000,45.637800,473.132000,288.419000,473.132000,45.637800,458.932000,288.419000,458.932000,45.637800,460.132000,288.450000,460.132000,45.637800,445.932000,288.450000,445.932000,45.637800,447.132000,288.450000,447.132000,45.637800,432.932000,288.450000,432.932000,45.637800,434.132000,166.429000,434.132000,45.637800,419.932000,166.429000,419.932000" rect="45.194000,419.489000,288.893000,603.576000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The&#xD;findings highlight the need to share information about the&#xD;temporal nature of mental fatigue and mental recovery of&#xD;athletes with practitioners and co-design&#xD;of research to&#xD;answer practitioner driven questions. Both researchers&#xD;and practitioners can collaborate meaningfully to share&#xD;knowledge and evidence-based&#xD;practice. </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Figure 5 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>provides&#xD;a summary of current practices shared by respondents&#xD;and relevant available evidence for practitioners. Lastly,&#xD;coaches and practitioners can adopt a multi-disciplinary&#xD;approach to the consistent assessment and management&#xD;of mental fatigue and mental recovery of their athletes in&#xD;a periodized manner to support outcomes in training and&#xD;performance in competition.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="12" rect="595.276000,511.132000,779.276000,603.132000"
/></highlight
